==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From Old (and modern) {{etyl|fr}} ''[[turbot#French|turbot]]'', from {{etyl|gmq-osw}} ''[[tornbut]]'', from ''[[törn]]'' (“thorn”) + ''[[but]]'' (“butt, flatfish”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɜːbət/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=turbot|pl2=turbots}}

# Any of various [[flatfish]]es of family ''Scophthalmidae'' that are found in marine or brackish waters.

